NOTE (crash FIX, asm-verified, proven to eliminate the t=43515 SIGSEGV): 77cf + b767 are base-lost weapon-
spawn siblings of 778a/b73b (patch 438).  7e29 dispatches 77cf for a second weapon; Ghidra host-ptr-deref'd
the FIRER near-offset (param_4) and used unaff_CS (garbage) for the b1df-spawned projectile -> SIGSEGV in
FUN_1000_77cf @ fist.c:59713 the moment a unit fires that weapon (caught via gdb; #1 was 7e29).  Fix mirrors
patch 438's 778a.  asm 0x1778a-sibling verified: [di+0xb3] ammo (WORD), [di+0xea]=3, b1df(0xa,di), b767(
proj,firer), [di+0xa8]=0x14, 9b5c(di), c047(0xc), [di+0x3c]=0x10, [di+0x92]=0.  With it the AZER1 self-play
runs 250s sim WITHOUT the crash (was SIGSEGV ~t=43515).

--- FUN_1000_77cf ---
void __allregs
FUN_1000_77cf(undefined2 param_1,undefined4 param_2,undefined4 param_3,int param_4,
             undefined2 param_5)

{
  /* PATCH 442: weapon-spawn method (asm 0x1778a sibling; DS=DGROUP).  di=param_4=FIRER near-offset; ammo
     WORD[di+0xb3]>0: dec ammo, [di+0xea]=3, a265(di), si=b1df(0xa,di) (CF=pool-cap -> stc/fail), b767(
     firer,proj), firer reload [di+0xa8]=0x14, 9b5c(di), c047, [di+0x3c]=0x10, clear [di+0x92].  Ghidra
     host-ptr-deref'd di, int-widened the WORD ammo, and used unaff_CS (garbage) for the post-writes
     (SIGSEGV in 7e29's fire path). Mirrors patch 438's 778a. */
  extern unsigned char g_fist_cf;
  unsigned char *dg = (unsigned char *)g_mem + 0x1c000;
  unsigned short di = (unsigned short)param_4;
  if (*(unsigned short *)(dg + (unsigned short)(di + 0xb3)) != 0) {
    *(unsigned short *)(dg + (unsigned short)(di + 0xb3)) -= 1;
    dg[(unsigned short)(di + 0xea)] = 3;
    FUN_1000_a265(param_1,param_2,(int)di);
    { unsigned short si = (unsigned short)FUN_1000_b1df(0xa,(int *)(uintptr_t)di);
      if (g_fist_cf) { g_fist_cf = 1; return; }
      FUN_0000_b767((undefined2)param_2,(int)si,(int)di,param_5);
      dg[(unsigned short)(di + 0xa8)] = 0x14;
      FUN_0000_9b5c((int)di);
      FUN_0000_c047(0xc,param_3,(int)di);
      dg[(unsigned short)(di + 0x3c)] = 0x10;
      dg[(unsigned short)(di + 0x92)] = 0; }
  }
  return;
}

